        "id": "s3",
        "title": "Mathematical Formalization of Forensic Breach Metrics: Total Mean Time to Remediate (MTTR)",
        "type": "equation",
        "solo": {
          "speaker": "Dr. Nova (Senior Architect)",
          "title": "Mathematical Formalization of Forensic Breach Metrics: Total Mean Time to Remediate (MTTR)",
          "turns": [
            {
              "speaker": "Dr. Nova",
              "text": "Mathematical Formalization of Forensic Breach Metrics: Total Mean Time to Remediate (MTTR). Formalizing the empirical sample mathematically reveals that empirical risk only approximates true generalization risk when the i.i.d. assumption holds. When upstream sampling is biased, the empirical risk diverges asymptotically from true risk—no model tuning can fix that."
            }
          ],
          "contentHtml": "<div class=\"p-3.5 rounded-xl bg-[#fffdf7] border-2 border-[#151b20] shadow-[3px_3px_0px_#151b20] my-2 text-center\">\n  <div class=\"text-[10px] font-mono text-[#0e7490] font-black uppercase tracking-wider mb-1 text-left flex items-center justify-between\">\n    <span>📐 Mathematical Formulation</span>\n    <span class=\"text-[#151b20] text-[9px] font-mono bg-[#eee4c8] px-2 py-0.5 rounded border border-[#151b20]\">Empirical Sample Formulation</span>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"text-base md:text-lg font-serif text-[#151b20] py-1 overflow-x-auto bg-[#f0fbfd] border border-[#0e7490] rounded-lg my-1\">\n    $$t_{\\text{MTTR}} = t_{\\text{dwell}} + t_{\\text{containment}} = \\left( t_{\\text{detection}} - t_{\\text{infiltrate}} \\right) + \\left( t_{\\text{containment}} - t_{\\text{detection}} \\right)$$\n  </div>\n</div>"
        },
